---
// Seat routing, once you add a second worker: Clef makes one choice per work package.
---

<div class="pl-wrap">
  <div class="pl-routing">
    <div class="fx-node fx-in" data-c="grey" style="--d:0">
      Work package<small>from the Architect's plan</small>
    </div>
    <span class="fx-arrow fx-in" style="--d:300" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="fx-node fx-in" data-c="amber" style="--d:450">
      Clef<small>one choice · bar 0.85</small>
    </div>
    <span class="fx-arrow fx-in" style="--d:750" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="pl-branches">
      <div class="pl-branch fx-in" data-c="green" style="--d:900">
        <span class="pl-out" data-c="green">
          at 0.85 or more · e.g. 0.91
        </span>
        <div class="fx-node" data-c="teal">
          Cheapest worker that fits<small>its criteria clearly met</small>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pl-branch fx-in" data-c="grey" style="--d:1300">
        <span class="pl-out" data-c="grey">
          under 0.85 · e.g. 0.72
        </span>
        <div class="fx-node" data-c="teal">
          Configured worker<small>last in the list · the default</small>
        </div>
        <span class="pl-when">
          Also keeps the package when the Architect set a reasoning minimum,
          evidence is missing, or the risk is high.
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="pl-routing-foot fx-in" style="--d:1700">
    <span class="fx-chip" data-c="grey" data-wrap>
      Architect and judge: never routed
    </span>
    <span class="fx-chip" data-c="grey" data-wrap>
      one worker, as shipped: nothing to pick
    </span>
  </div>
</div>
